 on LAST_PASS_REF) and the read-path caller last_pass._read_record (line 168, ref_lock._read_blob_bytes). The plan hand-lists callers as 'acquire, release, heartbeat, set_gate and set_pause' and claims '_object_type receives _REMOTE_TIMEOUT_SECS from every caller', but a symbol/grep sweep shows last_pass.py reaches both _cas_advance and _read_blob_bytes on a refs/reconciler/* ref that can carry a legacy blob tip and lazily fetch.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f065712c997cdb37e","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach: '_object_type (cat-file -t <oid>) for ALL its callers — the read path, and the write path _cas_advance reached from acquire, release, heartbeat, set_gate and set_pause'; AC: '_object_type receives _REMOTE_TIMEOUT_SECS from every caller, asserted by the same test on the read path and during a set_gate CAS advance'","norm_id":"n9e13ee9f8bb672e2","priority":0.165,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["last_pass.record_pass (last_pass.py:330) CAS-advances LAST_PASS_REF over a legacy blob tip in a blobless clone, triggering a lazy promisor fetch in _object_type that the plan's caller reasoning and AC do not acknowledge or test — the 'every caller' claim is unverified for this path.","last_pass._read_record (last_pass.py:168) reads the last-pass blob via _read_blob_bytes on a blobless clone; the plan's AC does not cover this read path, so a regression reintroducing a local budget on a path reachable from last_pass would go uncaught."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Re-derive the caller set with find_referencing_symbols on _cas_advance and _read_blob_bytes; add last_pass.record_pass and last_pass._read_record to the Approach enumeration and either state the fix is at the _OBJ_READ_SECS definition level (so all callers inherit it) or add a test asserting the remote budget on the last_pass CAS-advance path.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted